Evaluation — Frontend Remix v1.1.0 (5-style replacement)
Automated checks (re-verified)
54 files in build dir (excluding `.forge/`), no empty sources.

`manifest.json` valid JSON, name=Frontend Remix, version=1.1.0, MV3, `web_accessible_resources` exposes `assets/*`, `assets/*/*`, `assets/*/*/*` to `<all_urls>`.

All 4 JS files parse cleanly (style-engine, content, background, popup).

Checklist vs DESIGN.md / PLAN.md

RequirementStatusEvidence5 new styles replace oldPASS`assets/` contains exactly `brutalism`, `swiss`, `bento`, `editorial`, `retro-y2k`; no legacy dirs remain.Per-style fonts/borders/buttons/spacing/layout CSSPASSAll 5 styles have all 5 CSS files (26–46 lines each).Per-style icons/*.svg bundled locallyPASSEach style dir has all 4 SVGs (arrow/check/close/settings), valid `<svg xmlns=...>`.Palette tokens match briefPASSEach `fonts.css` defines exactly the brief's custom properties.Brief rules (3px+6px shadow brutalism, 0-radius swiss, 24px bento tiles, hairline editorial, pill/glassy/neon y2k)PASSVerified in each `borders.css` / `buttons.css` / `layout.css`.Dropdown selecting the 5 stylesPASS`popup.html` `#frx-style-picker` + `#frx-style-clear`; `popup.js` `STYLES`, `populateStylePicker()`, change → `FRX_APPLY_STYLE`, clear → `FRX_CLEAR_STYLE`, `syncStyle()` → `FRX_GET_STYLE`.Content script injects CSS/icons from `chrome-extension://`PASS`style-engine.js` `assetUrl()` via `runtime.getURL`, `injectCss()` fetch→inline `<style>` with `<link>` fallback, `applyIcons()`, `tagIcons()` sets `--frx-icon-*` + `data-frx-style`.Message contract wired end-to-endPASSAll 11 message types present across content + background.Font-swap feature intactPASSScan / FontFace-from-bytes / data-URL fallback / `FRX_BG_FETCH_FONT` Google-CSS + direct-file / system-font detection unchanged.AA contrast, reduced-motion, responsive, tokens-firstPASSTokens-first `:root` in every `fonts.css`; `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` in all 5 `buttons.css`; responsive `@media (max-width:768px)` in every `layout.css`.
Minor observations (polish only)
Style selection not persisted via `chrome.storage` — per-tab only, re-synced on popup open. Brief didn't require cross-tab persistence.

`applyIcons` uses `rel=preload` as a side-channel; actual icons flow through `--frx-icon-*` custom properties. Works, but generates unused-preload DevTools noise.

Editorial `h1` fixed 72px / 44px mobile is inside the 64–120px spec but could `clamp()`.

Next steps
`content/content.js` + `popup/popup.js` — persist chosen style per-origin via `chrome.storage.local` (`frx:style:<origin>`); on content-script init read storage and re-apply; popup should show stored value when `FRX_GET_STYLE` returns `''`. Most likely user-facing gap.

`content/style-engine.js` — replace `preload`-only `applyIcons()` with a single generated `<style>` setting `--frx-icon-*` directly, removing unused-preload console noise.

`assets/editorial/fonts.css` — convert `h1` fixed sizing to `clamp(44px, 7vw, 96px)` to track the 64–120px brief range across viewports.

`assets/brutalism/borders.css` — scope the universal `img { border:3px solid; box-shadow:6px 6px 0 }` (e.g. to interactive/media tiles) to avoid wrecking image-heavy pages.

`popup/popup.js` — debounce/disable `#frx-refresh` while a scan is in flight; disable `#frx-style-clear` when `currentStyle === ''`.

`.forge/PLAN.md` — record the storage-persistence decision once step 1 lands.

